## Metrics to publish

The Lisbon Best AI Tooling winner won on a measurement (30x token reduction across 30 live subgraphs). Bring a table nobody else brings.

Test suite = the metrics. Foundry fuzz on the invariant, plus 12 named escalation scenarios:

| # | Attack | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Child sets capability bit parent lacks | `SCOPE_WIDENED` |
| 2 | Child spendCap > parent remaining | `CAP_EXCEEDS_UNALLOCATED` |
| 3 | Child expiry beyond parent | `EXPIRY_EXTENDED` |
| 4 | Grandchild re-adds a bit parent dropped | `SCOPE_WIDENED` |
| 5 | Child de-escalates readOnly | `READONLY_ESCALATION` |
| 6 | Delegate past maxDepth | `DEPTH_EXCEEDED` |
| 7 | Execute after root revoked | `REVOKED_OR_EXPIRED` |
| 8 | Two children each granted full parent budget | second reverts |
| 9 | Non-agent calls execute | `NOT_AGENT` |
| 10 | Capability bit valid, target wrong | `TARGET_MISMATCH` |
| 11 | Grant from address without `ROLE_GRANT` | `NOT_GRANTOR` |
| 12 | Grant under a revoked parent | `PARENT_DEAD` |

Also publish: max delegation depth, gas per grant, gas per revocation, root-to-leaf revocation latency, Substreams trigger lag vs polling.

