## Submission checklist

**Deadline: Sun 13 Sep 2026, 12:00 pm EDT = 9:30 pm IST. Submit by 9:30 am IST.**

- [ ] Public GitHub repo, open source, clear README
- [ ] `AI-USE.md` — where and how AI tools were used, per file/directory (**required**)
- [ ] `SPEC.md` and `prompts/` committed to the repo (**required for spec-driven workflows**)
- [ ] Small, frequent commits from all three people — no single large dump
- [ ] README distinguishes our work from libraries and starter kits
- [ ] Demo video 2–4 minutes, **720p or higher**, human narration, not phone-recorded, not sped up
- [ ] Three partner write-ups drafted in advance: integration explanation + feedback + comments, one per partner
- [ ] Built on `wallet-cli ring` (Ledger)
- [ ] Remote Key Ring enrollment working on a VPS with no USB port (Ledger — their second ask)
- [ ] Three device touchpoints, not one (Ledger)
- [ ] Device counterfactual shot in the video — same escalation with and without the device
- [ ] ENSv2 on Sepolia, no hard-coded values (ENS)
- [ ] Wildcard resolution + non-transferable flags + split EAC roles (ENS)
- [ ] Name resolves in an external ENS client, on camera (ENS)
- [ ] Own subgraph deployed and indexing the permission tree (Graph)
- [ ] Substreams gRPC with cursor resumption and reorg handling (Graph)
- [ ] Substreams-vs-polling benchmark with missed-event count (Graph)
- [ ] Live Graph data with real API key, **Start Fresh** pool (Graph)
- [ ] `FEEDBACK.md` for Ledger DX
- [ ] `SKILL.md` for the MCP server, published and usable standalone
- [ ] Metrics table in README and on the landing page
- [ ] Prior-art paragraph naming ENSFirewall and WorkAgnt honestly
- [ ] Three partner prizes selected on the ETHGlobal platform

